ngs from pairs, or Seven Pairs suggests retaining critical pairs and sequence-building tiles (W2/W3 for chow potential). T8 is isolated with no adjacent tiles (no T7/T9), making it the weakest candidate for future melds. Discarding T8 preserves stronger structural elements while minimizing deadwood.\n\nReason: T8 lacks connectivity in Bamboo suit and offers minimal contribution to potential patterns. Keeping T3 pair (for possible pung/all-pungs), J2 pair (Dragon Pung value), and W2/W3 (chow foundation) aligns better with scoring opportunities. Terminals like W9/B9 retain slight terminal-pattern utility, but T8\u2019s mid-simple status provides no strategic advantage here.\n\nAnswer: Play T8"}
